#[local] Existing Instance edgeset.

(*
   * * The walking commutative square, by generators and relations

   nLab: https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/commutative+square
   nLab: https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/free+category
   Book: Mac Lane, Categories for the Working Mathematician, 2nd ed.,
   §II.8, printed p. 52 (Exercise 1: describe the category
   generated by the square diagram subject to commutativity, and
   count its arrows)
   Book: Riehl, Category Theory in Context, Dover 2016, §1.6,
   Example 1.6.6 (printed p. 41: the commutative square as the
   shape 2 × 2) and Example 1.6.9 (printed p. 42: the shape
   2 × 3 and commutative rectangles)
   Book: Fong and Spivak, Seven Sketches in Compositionality, CUP 2019,
   §3.2.2 (finite presentations of categories)

   Mac Lane's exercise names a diagram — four objects, four arrows
   arranged in a square — and asks for the category it generates once
   the square is required to commute.  The answer he wants is a count:
   nine arrows, four of them identities.  The fifth non-identity arrow
   is the diagonal, and the whole point of the exercise is that it is
   NOT a fifth generator: it is the common value of the two composites,
   and the single imposed relation is exactly what makes those two
   composites one arrow rather than two.

   This file builds that category as a finite presentation over
   [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v], proves the count, and
   records the shape's universal property: a functor out of it is a
   commutative square in the target, and nothing else.

   WHAT IS DELIVERED HERE.  (1) the presentation [SquarePresentation]
   and the category [Square], with the relation holding
   ([square_commutes]) and the diagonal identified as the common
   composite ([square_diagonal_via_B], [square_diagonal_via_C]);
   (2) a classification of every PATH of the underlying free category
   by its endpoints, at LEIBNIZ strength ([wsq_classify] — the free
   hom-sets are enumerated on the nose, not merely up to [≈]), from
   which everything else follows; (3) thinness of [Square]
   ([Square_Thin]), the absence of nontrivial endomorphisms
   ([square_endo_id]) and emptiness of the seven hom-sets that carry no
   arrow ([square_no_hom_BA] and its six siblings); (4) the arrow count,
   both as a duplicate-free enumeration of the nine inhabited endpoint
   pairs with soundness and completeness, and as a number folded over
   all sixteen pairs ([square_arrow_total] = 9,
   [square_identity_total] = 4,
   [square_nonidentity_total] = 5); (5) the same count for the FREE
   square ([free_square_arrow_total] = 10), so the quotient is measured
   to merge exactly one pair and nothing else; (6) the index-shape
   reading, [Square ⟶ C] against [CommutingSquare C] with both round
   trips and the universal property; (7) the identification of a
   commutative square with a MORPHISM of the arrow category
   ([Construction/Arrow.v]), in both directions.

   Checkbox A of the issue — the identification with 2 × 2 — is
   [Instance/Square/Product.v]; checkbox B — the shape 2 × 3 and
   commutative rectangles — is [Instance/Square/Rectangle.v].

   WHY THE COUNT IS THE SUBSTANTIAL HALF, and how it is kept honest.
   An arrow count in a presented category is a statement about
   [≈]-classes, and a quotient can always collapse further than
   intended; a count proved by collapse would be worthless.  Four
   separate facts keep this one from being vacuous.  First, the free
   count is proved TOO: [free_square_arrow_total] = 10 against
   [square_arrow_total] = 9, so exactly one identification happened.
   Second, that identification is exhibited on both sides — the two
   diagonals are provably DISTINCT in the free category
   ([free_square_diagonals_distinct], already in
   [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v]) and provably EQUAL in the
   presented one ([square_relation_holds]).  Third, the diagonal is
   proved to be a composite and not a generator: the quiver has exactly
   four edges ([square_generator_total] = 4, computed from the
   [FiniteQuiver] data), while the presented category has five
   non-identity arrows.  Fourth, and independently of the
   classification the other three route through, the shape carries two
   numerical invariants: a RANK that re-derives five of the seven empty
   hom-sets by arithmetic alone, and a path LENGTH that is invariant
   under the imposed congruence ([square_length_invariant], proved by
   induction on [CongClosure] and using neither [wsq_classify] nor
   [Square_Thin]), so that the diagonal is a two-step path at EVERY
   representative ([square_diagonal_is_two_steps]) while every
   generator is one step.  That paragraph's own limits are stated where
   the invariants are proved.

   THE CLASSIFICATION IS AT LEIBNIZ STRENGTH, deliberately.  The edges
   of [SquareQuiver] carry the standard [eq] setoid
   ([Build_Quiver_Standard_Eq]), so [wsq_classify] can and does
   conclude a Leibniz equality of paths rather than a [tlist]
   equivalence — every path from A to D IS [square_diag_fh] or IS
   [square_diag_gk], on the nose.  That is stronger than the [≈]-level
   statement and it is what makes the free count a count of ARROWS
   rather than of classes.  Only the presented statements descend to
   [≈], because only there is [≈] coarser than [=].

   TWO SQUARE SHAPES ALREADY EXIST IN THE TREE, and the reader should
   not confuse them with this one or with each other.
   [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v] declares [SquareQuiver] over
   [SquareNode]/[SquareEdge] with the four edges NAMED [Sq_f], [Sq_g],
   [Sq_h], [Sq_k]; that is the quiver this file presents, reused rather
   than redeclared, along with its [square_diag_fh]/[square_diag_gk]
   and the negative result [free_square_diagonals_distinct] that file
   already proves.  [Theory/Diagram.v] declares a DIFFERENT quiver
   under the SAME name [SquareQuiver], over [SqNode] with anonymous
   unit-valued edges, serving the diagram-commutativity development
   there ([square_commutative_iff], [sq_len_rank]).  The two names
   collide, harmlessly, because no file imports both; this one imports
   the [Construction/] quiver and not [Theory/Diagram.v].  That file's
   [sq_paths] is the independent shadow of [wsq_classify] one level
   down: it classifies the DENOTATIONS of paths in a target category
   under a commutativity hypothesis, whereas [wsq_classify] classifies
   the paths themselves, in the free category, with no hypothesis and
   at Leibniz equality.  Its [sq_len_rank] rank argument is the other
   standard route to the same classification, and is NOT the route
   taken here — the induction below is direct, and the seven empty
   hom-sets fall out of it rather than out of a rank inequality.
   Finally, [Construction/Sq.v] is unrelated: it is the double category
   of commuting squares in an ambient category.

   A UNIVERSE PIN IN THE DONOR WAS LIFTED to make this file's clause
   (6) general, and the lift is the one
   [Construction/Free/Quiver/Examples.v]'s header had diagnosed and
   called out of scope.  [Build_Quiver_Standard_Eq]
   ([Construction/Free/Quiver.v]) elaborated to [Quiver@{u u0 Set}]:
   its edge setoid's PROOF universe minimized to [Set], because it was
   built from [Corelib.Classes.CRelationClasses.eq_equivalence@{u}],
   which carries one universe binder and cannot separate the carrier's
   level from the proof level.  Since [InducedFunctor] identifies the
   TARGET category's hom and proof universes with the quiver's, every
   functor out of a free or presented category was confined to a target
   [Category@{o Set Set}] — measured by probe, not inferred:
   [InducedFunctor SquareQuiver F] into [Instance/Coq.v]'s [Coq] was a
   universe inconsistency.  The constructor now names its proof
   universe and spends the polymorphism of Lib/Setoid.v's own
   [eq_equivalence@{t u}], introduced for exactly this purpose, so
   [SquareFunctor] and [square_universal] below apply at an arbitrary
   target.  Test/ProbeSquare.v is the standing guard, and
   Construction/Free/Quiver/Examples.v's header carries the erratum.

   THREE CORRECTIONS to the catalogue entry this file answers, each
   measured against the tree rather than inherited from the issue text.
   (i) The issue proposes [Theory/Metacategory.v]'s [Three] as the
   linear order on three objects, for the 2 × 3 shape.  [Three] HAS NO
   OBJECTS — that file's own header says so in terms —
   so the product would be objectless.  The three-object linear
   category to use is [Instance/Ordinal.v]'s [_3 := Ordinal 3], and
   [Instance/Square/Rectangle.v] uses it.  (ii) The issue states that
   no presented finite category is built anywhere in the tree.  That is
   false: [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v] presents the
   commutative TRIANGLE, with both halves proved ([ord3_free_distinct]
   and [ord3_relation_holds]).  This square is its sibling and reuses
   its machinery verbatim.  (iii) The issue's roster of finite shapes
   in [Instance/] omits [Instance/Ordinal.v], which supplies the whole
   [Ordinal n] family.  What does hold is the central absence claim:
   before this file there was no walking commutative square anywhere in
   the tree.

   WHAT IS NOT DELIVERED.  No decision procedure on the hom-sets of
   [Square] is exported: the classification is a proof by induction on
   paths, and no [ObjDecEq]/hom-decidability instance is registered.
   No comparison with [Construction/Funny.v]'s [_2 □ _2] is made (the
   two shapes differ precisely by the interchange law, and the tree
   carries no comparison functor).  No claim is made that [Square] is
   the free category on any OTHER presentation of the same shape. 

   --------
   * * 步行交换方格，通过生成元和关系  

   nLab:  https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/commutative+square  
   nLab:  https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/free+category  
   书籍: Mac Lane，《为工作数学家准备的范畴论》，第2版，  
   §II.8，第52页印刷版（练习1：描述由方格图生成且受交换性约束的范畴，并计算其箭头数量）  
   书籍: Riehl，《语境中的范畴论》，Dover 2016，§1.6，  
   示例1.6.6（第41页印刷版：作为2 × 2形状的交换方格）和示例1.6.9（第42页印刷版：2 × 3形状和交换矩形）  
   书籍: Fong 和 Spivak，《组合性中的七个草图》，CUP 2019，  
   §3.2.2（范畴的有限表示）麦克·莱恩的练习命名了一个图——四个对象、四条箭头排列成一个正方形——并要求在该正方形必须交换的情况下生成的范畴。他想要的答案是一个计数：九条箭头，其中四条是恒等箭头。第五条非恒等箭头是对角线，而这个练习的全部重点在于它不是第五个生成元：它是两个复合箭头的共同值，唯一施加的关系正是使这两个复合箭头成为一个箭头而不是两个箭头的原因。

   这个文件将该范畴作为 [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v] 上的有限表示构建，证明了计数，并记录了该形状的泛性性质：从它出的函子是在目标中的交换正方形，而没有其他的东西。这里交付的是什么。(1) 表示 [SquarePresentation] 和范畴 [Square]，关系成立 ([square_commutes])，对角线被识别为公共复合 ([square_diagonal_via_B], [square_diagonal_via_C])；
   (2) 按其端点对基础自由范畴的每条路径进行分类，以 LEIBNIZ 强度（[wsq_classify] — 自由同态集合是精确枚举的，而不仅仅是到 [≈] 的同构），由此衍生出其他一切；
   (3) [Square] 的薄性 ([Square_Thin])、不存在非平凡自同态 ([square_endo_id]) 以及七个没有箭头的同态集合为空 ([square_no_hom_BA] 及其六个兄弟)；
   (4) 箭头计数，既作为九个存在的端点对的无重复枚举，并保证健全性与完备性，也作为对所有十六对端点折叠后的数值 ([square_arrow_total] = 9, [square_identity_total] = 4,[square_nonidentity_total] = 5); (5) 自由方格（[free_square_arrow_total] = 10）也有相同的计数，因此商被测量为正好合并一对而不多于一对；(6) 指数-形状读数，[Square ⟶ C] 对照 [CommutingSquare C]，具有往返和普遍性；(7) 将交换方格识别为箭头范畴的一个态射（[Construction/Arrow.v]），在两个方向上。问题的复选框 A——与 2 × 2 的识别——是 [Instance/Square/Product.v]；复选框 B——形状 2 × 3 和可交换矩形——是 [Instance/Square/Rectangle.v]。为什么计数是实质上的一半，以及它如何保持可靠。在一个给定范畴中的箭头计数是关于 [≈] 类的陈述，而商可以总是比预期的进一步塌缩；通过塌缩证明的计数将毫无价值。四个独立的事实使这个计数不至于空洞。首先，自由计数也得到了证明：[free_square_arrow_total] = 10 对比 [square_arrow_total] = 9，所以恰好发生了一次同一性。第二，这个同一性在两边都有体现——在自由范畴中两条对角线是可证明不同的（[free_square_diagonals_distinct]，已经在 [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v] 中出现）并且在给定范畴中是可证明相等的（[square_relation_holds]）。第三，证明了对角线是一个复合而非生成元：这个箭袋正好有四条边（[square_generator_total] = 4，根据[FiniteQuiver] 数据计算），而呈现的范畴有五条非同一箭。第四，并且独立于其他三条路径通过的分类，这个形状具有两个数值不变量：一个秩（RANK），仅通过算术就重新导出了七个空同态集中的五个；以及一个路径长度（LENGTH），在施加的同余下保持不变（[square_length_invariant]，通过对[CongClosure] 的归纳证明，并且未使用 [wsq_classify] 或 [Square_Thin]），因此对角线在每一个代表处都是两步路径（[square_diagonal_is_two_steps]），而每个生成元都是一步。该段落的自身局限性在证明不变量时已经说明。分类在莱布尼茨强度上，是故意的。[SquareQuiver] 的边携带标准的 [eq] 集合（[Build_Quiver_Standard_Eq]），因此 [wsq_classify] 可以并且确实得出路径的莱布尼茨等同性，而不是 [tlist] 等价——从 A 到 D 的每条路径要么是 [square_diag_fh]，要么是 [square_diag_gk]，完全一致。这比 [≈] 级别的陈述更强，并且这正是使自由计数成为箭头计数而非类计数的原因。只有所展示的陈述可以下降到 [≈]，因为只有在那里 [≈] 比 [=] 更粗。树中已经存在两个正方形，读者不应将它们与这个正方形或相互混淆。[Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v] 在 [SquareNode] / [SquareEdge] 上声明 [SquareQuiver]，并将四条边命名为 [Sq_f]、[Sq_g]、[Sq_h]、[Sq_k]；这是本文件呈现的箭图，被重复使用而不是重新声明，以及它的 [square_diag_fh] / [square_diag_gk] 和该文件已经证明的负结果 [free_square_diagonals_distinct]。[Theory/Diagram.v] 在相同名称 [SquareQuiver] 下声明了一个不同的箭图，作用于 [SqNode]，其边具有匿名单位值，用于那里的图交换性发展（[square_commutative_iff]、[sq_len_rank]）。这两个名称碰撞是无害的，因为没有文件同时导入两者；本文件导入 [Construction/] 箭图而不导入 [Theory/Diagram.v]。该文件的 [sq_paths] 是 [wsq_classify] 的独立影子，比它低一级：它在交换性假设下对目标范畴中路径的指称进行分类，而 [wsq_classify] 则在自由范畴中对路径本身进行分类，没有任何假设，并且在莱布尼茨等式下其 [sq_len_rank] 的秩论证是达到相同分类的另一标准路线，而这里并未采用——下面的归纳是直接进行的，七个空同态集是由此而自然得出，而不是由秩不等式得出。最后，ZWZ69WZZ 无关：它是一个环境范畴中交换方格的双范畴。捐赠者中的一个宇宙针被提升，以使此文件的条款(6)变得通用，而提升的那个是[Construction/Free/Quiver/Examples.v]的头文件已经诊断并标记为超出范围。[Build_Quiver_Standard_Eq]（[Construction/Free/Quiver.v]）向[Quiver@{u u0 Set}]详细说明：其边缘集合体的PROOF宇宙被最小化为[Set]，因为它是由[Corelib.Classes.CRelationClasses.eq_equivalence@{u}]构建的，[Corelib.Classes.CRelationClasses.eq_equivalence@{u}]携带一个宇宙绑定器，无法将载体的层级与证明层级分开。由于[InducedFunctor]将目标类别的hom和证明宇宙与箭头集的宇宙识别为同一，因此从自由或呈现类别出的每个函子都被限制在目标[Category@{o Set Set}]——通过探测测量，而不是推断：[InducedFunctor SquareQuiver F]进入[Instance/Coq.v]的[Coq]时出现了宇宙不一致。构造函数现在命名其证明宇宙，并利用 Lib/Setoid.v 自身的 [eq_equivalence@{t u}] 的多态性，这正是为此目的引入的，因此下面的 [SquareFunctor] 和 [square_universal] 可以应用于任意目标。Test/ProbeSquare.v 是常驻守卫，而 Construction/Free/Quiver/Examples.v 的标题带有勘误。对该文件回答的目录条目有三处修正，每一处都是针对树本身而非从期刊文本继承的。(i) 期刊提出 [Theory/Metacategory.v] 的 [Three] 作为三对象的线性顺序，用于 2 × 3 形状。[Three] 没有对象——该文件自己的标题也明确说明——所以此乘积将没有对象。要使用的三对象线性范畴是 [Instance/Ordinal.v] 的 [_3 := Ordinal 3]，[Instance/Square/Rectangle.v] 使用了它。(ii) 期刊声明没有呈现的有限范畴是在树的任何地方构建的。这是错误的：[Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v] 呈现了交换三角形，其两个部分都已证明（[ord3_free_distinct] 和 [ord3_relation_holds]）。这个方形是它的同级，并完全复用了它的机制。(iii) 该问题的有限形状列表在 [Instance/] 中省略了 [Instance/Ordinal.v]，而后者提供了整个 [Ordinal n] 系列。确实成立的是中心缺失声明：在此文件之前，树中不存在任何行走交换方形。

   未提供的内容。没有导出 [Square] 的同态集的判定程序：该分类是基于路径的归纳证明，并且没有注册任何 [ObjDecEq] /同态可判定性实例。没有与 [Construction/Funny.v] 的 [_2 □ _2] 进行比较（这两种形状的差异恰恰在于交换律，并且树中没有比较函子）。也没有声称 [Square] 是任意其他同形状表现的自由范畴。
*)

(*
   * ** The free category on the square quiver

   [SquareQuiver], its nodes and its four named edges are
   [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v]'s, and so are the two
   diagonal paths [square_diag_fh] and [square_diag_gk]. 

   --------
   * ** 正方形箭袋上的自由范畴

   [SquareQuiver]，其节点及其四条命名边
   [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v] 的，两个对角路径 [square_diag_fh] 和 [square_diag_gk] 也是如此。
*)

Definition FreeSquare : Category := FreeOnQuiver SquareQuiver.

(** The four generating edges, as one-step paths of the free category. / 四条生成边，作为自由范畴的一步路径。 *)
Definition wsq_f : Sq_A ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_B :=
  tlist_singleton (B:=@edges SquareQuiver) Sq_f.
Definition wsq_g : Sq_A ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_C :=
  tlist_singleton (B:=@edges SquareQuiver) Sq_g.
Definition wsq_h : Sq_B ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_D :=
  tlist_singleton (B:=@edges SquareQuiver) Sq_h.
Definition wsq_k : Sq_C ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_D :=
  tlist_singleton (B:=@edges SquareQuiver) Sq_k.

(*
   * Composition of one-step paths IS the two-step path, definitionally —
   composition in [FreeOnQuiver] is [tlist] concatenation with the
   arguments flipped.  Recorded as a Leibniz equality because the two
   sides are the very same term after reduction; this is the
   convention documented at [Functor/Bifunctor.v]. 

   --------
   * 一步路径的复合从定义上就是两步路径——
   在 [FreeOnQuiver] 中的复合是 [tlist] 的连接，但参数顺序翻转。
   记录为 Leibniz 等式，因为约简后两边是完全相同的项；这是在 [Functor/Bifunctor.v] 中记录的约定。
*)
Example free_diag_fh_is_composite :
  @compose FreeSquare _ _ _ wsq_h wsq_f = square_diag_fh := eq_refl.

Example free_diag_gk_is_composite :
  @compose FreeSquare _ _ _ wsq_k wsq_g = square_diag_gk := eq_refl.

(*
   * ** Classifying every path by its endpoints

   The specification: for each ordered pair of nodes, exactly which
   paths join them.  [False] marks the seven pairs joined by no path at
   all.  The equalities are Leibniz, not [≈] — see the header. 

   --------
   * ** 按路径的端点对每条路径进行分类

   规范：对于每一个有序节点对，正好哪些路径将它们连接起来。[False] 标记了七对根本没有路径连接的节点。等式是莱布尼茨的，而不是 [≈] —— 见标题。
*)
Definition wsq_spec (y : SquareNode) :
  ∀ x : SquareNode, (x ~{FreeSquare}~> y) → Type :=
  match y as y0 return ∀ x : SquareNode, (x ~{FreeSquare}~> y0) → Type with
  | Sq_A => fun x => match x as x0 return (x0 ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_A) → Type with
      | Sq_A => fun p => p = tnil
      | Sq_B => fun _ => False
      | Sq_C => fun _ => False
      | Sq_D => fun _ => False
      end
  | Sq_B => fun x => match x as x0 return (x0 ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_B) → Type with
      | Sq_A => fun p => p = wsq_f
      | Sq_B => fun p => p = tnil
      | Sq_C => fun _ => False
      | Sq_D => fun _ => False
      end
  | Sq_C => fun x => match x as x0 return (x0 ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_C) → Type with
      | Sq_A => fun p => p = wsq_g
      | Sq_B => fun _ => False
      | Sq_C => fun p => p = tnil
      | Sq_D => fun _ => False
      end
  | Sq_D => fun x => match x as x0 return (x0 ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_D) → Type with
      | Sq_A => fun p => ((p = square_diag_fh) + (p = square_diag_gk))%type
      | Sq_B => fun p => p = wsq_h
      | Sq_C => fun p => p = wsq_k
      | Sq_D => fun p => p = tnil
      end
  end.

(*
   * Every path meets its specification.  One induction on the path: the
   empty path forces source and target to agree, and a step is one of
   the four edges, which pins the source and hands the rest to the
   induction hypothesis.  The two A → D branches are the only ones
   where the disjunction is entered, once on each side. 

   --------
   * 每条路径都满足其规范。对路径进行归纳：空路径强制源点和目标点一致，而一步是四条边之一，这确定了源点并将其余部分交给归纳假设。两个 A → D 分支是唯一进入析取的分支，每一侧各一次。
*)
Theorem wsq_classify (y x : SquareNode) (p : x ~{FreeSquare}~> y) :
  wsq_spec y x p.
Proof.
  induction p as [ | i j e p IH ].
  - destruct y; reflexivity.
  - destruct e; destruct y; simpl in *;
      try contradiction;
      try (rewrite IH; reflexivity).
    + left;  rewrite IH; reflexivity.
    + right; rewrite IH; reflexivity.
Qed.

(*
   * The seven empty hom-sets of the free square, read off the
   classification. 

   --------
   * 从分类中读出自由平方的七个空同态集合。
*)
Corollary free_square_no_path_BA (p : Sq_B ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_A) : False.
Proof. exact (wsq_classify _ _ p). Qed.

Corollary free_square_no_path_CA (p : Sq_C ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_A) : False.
Proof. exact (wsq_classify _ _ p). Qed.

Corollary free_square_no_path_DA (p : Sq_D ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_A) : False.
Proof. exact (wsq_classify _ _ p). Qed.

Corollary free_square_no_path_BC (p : Sq_B ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_C) : False.
Proof. exact (wsq_classify _ _ p). Qed.

Corollary free_square_no_path_CB (p : Sq_C ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_B) : False.
Proof. exact (wsq_classify _ _ p). Qed.

Corollary free_square_no_path_DB (p : Sq_D ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_B) : False.
Proof. exact (wsq_classify _ _ p). Qed.

Corollary free_square_no_path_DC (p : Sq_D ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_C) : False.
Proof. exact (wsq_classify _ _ p). Qed.

(*
   * ** The presentation

   Four nodes, four edges, ONE relation: the two diagonals agree.
   Finiteness is carried as data throughout, in the shape
   [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v] fixes — [Fin.t] indices with
   retractions, no existence claim over lists, hence no choice
   principle anywhere. 

   --------
   * ** 演示文稿

   四个节点，四条边，一个关系：两条对角线一致。
   有限性作为数据贯穿始终，在形状
   [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v]  固定 —  [Fin.t]  指数与
   收缩，没有关于列表的存在性声明，因此任何地方都没有选择原则。
*)

Definition SquareEqn_count (x y : SquareQuiver) : nat :=
  match x, y with Sq_A, Sq_D => 1 | _, _ => 0 end.

Definition SquareEqn_lhs (x y : SquareQuiver) :
  Fin.t (SquareEqn_count x y) → x ~{FreeSquare}~> y.
Proof.
  destruct x, y; simpl; intro i;
    solve [ exact (Fin.case0 _ i) | exact square_diag_fh ].
Defined.

Definition SquareEqn_rhs (x y : SquareQuiver) :
  Fin.t (SquareEqn_count x y) → x ~{FreeSquare}~> y.
Proof.
  destruct x, y; simpl; intro i;
    solve [ exact (Fin.case0 _ i) | exact square_diag_gk ].
Defined.

Definition SquareEqns : FiniteEquations SquareQuiver := {|
  fe_count := SquareEqn_count;
  fe_lhs   := SquareEqn_lhs;
  fe_rhs   := SquareEqn_rhs
|}.

(** The quiver is finite, with the enumeration carried as data. / 箭袋是有限的，枚举作为数据进行携带。 *)
Definition Square_node (i : Fin.t 4) : SquareNode :=
  match i with
  | Fin.F1 => Sq_A
  | Fin.FS j =>
      match j with
      | Fin.F1 => Sq_B
      | Fin.FS l =>
          match l with
          | Fin.F1 => Sq_C
          | Fin.FS _ => Sq_D
          end
      end
  end.

Definition Square_index (x : SquareNode) : Fin.t 4 :=
  match x with
  | Sq_A => Fin.F1
  | Sq_B => Fin.FS Fin.F1
  | Sq_C => Fin.FS (Fin.FS Fin.F1)
  | Sq_D => Fin.FS (Fin.FS (Fin.FS Fin.F1))
  end.

Lemma Square_node_rt (x : SquareNode) : Square_node (Square_index x) = x.
Proof. destruct x; reflexivity. Qed.

Definition Square_ecount (x y : SquareNode) : nat :=
  match x, y with
  | Sq_A, Sq_B => 1
  | Sq_A, Sq_C => 1
  | Sq_B, Sq_D => 1
  | Sq_C, Sq_D => 1
  | _, _ => 0
  end.

Definition Square_edge (x y : SquareNode) :
  Fin.t (Square_ecount x y) → SquareEdge x y.
Proof.
  destruct x, y; simpl; intro i;
    solve [ exact (Fin.case0 _ i)
          | exact Sq_f | exact Sq_g | exact Sq_h | exact Sq_k ].
Defined.

Definition Square_eindex (x y : SquareNode) (e : SquareEdge x y) :
  Fin.t (Square_ecount x y) :=
  match e in SquareEdge a b return Fin.t (Square_ecount a b) with
  | Sq_f => Fin.F1
  | Sq_g => Fin.F1
  | Sq_h => Fin.F1
  | Sq_k => Fin.F1
  end.

Lemma Square_edge_rt (x y : SquareNode) (e : SquareEdge x y) :
  Square_edge x y (Square_eindex x y e) = e.
Proof. destruct e; reflexivity. Qed.

Definition SquareFinite : FiniteQuiver SquareQuiver :=
  @Build_FiniteQuiver SquareQuiver 4 Square_node Square_index Square_node_rt
    Square_ecount Square_edge Square_eindex Square_edge_rt.

Definition SquarePresentation : FinitePresentation := {|
  fp_quiver := SquareQuiver;
  fp_finite := SquareFinite;
  fp_eqns   := SquareEqns
|}.

(** The walking commutative square. / 行走的交换方块。 *)
Definition Square : Category := FinitelyPresented SquarePresentation.

(*
   * ...which is the presented category of the quiver and the relation,
   definitionally. 

   --------
   * ……这就是箭袋及其关系的呈现类别，从定义上来说。
*)
Example Square_is_presented :
  Square = PresentedQuiver SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) := eq_refl.

(*
   * The hom TYPES of [Square] are the free ones: equations merge, and
   never add. 

   --------
   * [Square] 的同质类型是自由的：方程会合并，而不会增加。
*)
Example Square_hom_is_free (x y : SquareNode) :
  (x ~{Square}~> y) = (x ~{FreeSquare}~> y) := eq_refl.

(*
   * ** The generators, and the relation

   Mac Lane's exercise draws f and g on two sides of the square and
   f' and g' on the others; here they are [square_f] : A → B and
   [square_g] : A → C against [square_h] : B → D and [square_k] : C → D,
   keeping the names [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v] gave the
   edges. 

   --------
   * ** 生成元及其关系

   Mac Lane 的练习在正方形的两边绘制了 f 和 g，而在其他边上绘制了 f' 和 g'；它们分别是  [square_f]  : A → B 和  [square_g]  : A → C，与  [square_h]  : B → D 和  [square_k]  : C → D 对应，
   保留了  [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v]  给边的名称。
*)
Definition square_f : Sq_A ~{Square}~> Sq_B :=
  @pgen SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) _ _ Sq_f.
Definition square_g : Sq_A ~{Square}~> Sq_C :=
  @pgen SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) _ _ Sq_g.
Definition square_h : Sq_B ~{Square}~> Sq_D :=
  @pgen SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) _ _ Sq_h.
Definition square_k : Sq_C ~{Square}~> Sq_D :=
  @pgen SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) _ _ Sq_k.

(** The imposed equation holds. / 所施加的方程成立。 *)
Lemma square_relation_holds :
  @equiv _ (@homset Square Sq_A Sq_D) square_diag_fh square_diag_gk.
Proof. apply cc_gen. exists Fin.F1. split; reflexivity. Qed.

(*
   * The square commutes.  Both composites reduce to the corresponding
   two-step path definitionally, so this is [square_relation_holds]
   with no transport. 

   --------
   * 该方形可交换。 两个复合体都按照定义化简为相应的两步路径，因此这是 [square_relation_holds]， 无需传输。
*)
Theorem square_commutes :
  square_h ∘ square_f ≈ square_k ∘ square_g.
Proof. exact square_relation_holds. Qed.

(*
   * The diagonal: the common value of the two composites.  It is DEFINED
   as one of them, and proved equal to the other. 

   --------
   * 对角线：两个复合体的公共值。它被定义为其中之一，并被证明等于另一个。
*)
Definition square_diagonal : Sq_A ~{Square}~> Sq_D := square_h ∘ square_f.

Example square_diagonal_via_B : square_diagonal = square_h ∘ square_f := eq_refl.

Lemma square_diagonal_via_C : square_diagonal ≈ square_k ∘ square_g.
Proof. exact square_commutes. Qed.

(*
   * The diagonal is not a generator: the quiver has exactly four edges,
   computed from the [FiniteQuiver] data rather than asserted. 

   --------
   * 对角线不是生成元：箭矢图恰好有四条边，是根据 [FiniteQuiver] 数据计算得出的，而不是假定的。
*)
Definition square_generator_total : nat :=
  fold_right (fun q n => fq_edges SquareQuiver SquareFinite (fst q) (snd q) + n)%nat
             0%nat
    (list_prod (Sq_A :: Sq_B :: Sq_C :: Sq_D :: nil)
               (Sq_A :: Sq_B :: Sq_C :: Sq_D :: nil)).

Example square_generator_total_4 : square_generator_total = 4%nat := eq_refl.

(* * ** Thinness, and the empty hom-sets Everything below is read off [wsq_classify]. / * ** 稀薄性，以及空同态集 以下所有内容均取自 [wsq_classify] 。 *)

(*
   * Any two parallel arrows of [Square] agree.  The only case with
   anything to prove is A → D, where the two classified paths are
   identified by exactly the imposed relation. 

   --------
   * [Square] 中的任意两条平行箭头都相同。唯一需要证明的情况是 A → D，其中的两条分类路径正好通过所施加的关系被识别为相同。
*)
Theorem Square_Thin : Thin Square.
Proof.
  intros x y p q; destruct x, y;
    pose proof (wsq_classify _ _ p) as Hp;
    pose proof (wsq_classify _ _ q) as Hq;
    simpl in Hp, Hq;
    try contradiction;
    try (rewrite Hp, Hq; reflexivity).
  destruct Hp as [Hp|Hp], Hq as [Hq|Hq]; rewrite Hp, Hq.
  - reflexivity.
  - exact square_relation_holds.
  - symmetry; exact square_relation_holds.
  - reflexivity.
Qed.

(*
   * Every endomorphism is the identity: there are no nontrivial loops.
   This is what makes "four of the nine arrows are identities" a
   statement about arrows and not merely about endpoint pairs. 

   --------
   * 每一个自同态都是恒等映射：不存在非平凡的环路。
   这就是为什么“九个箭头中有四个是恒等箭头”是关于箭头的陈述，而不仅仅是关于端点对的原因。
*)
Corollary square_endo_id {x : Square} (p : x ~> x) : p ≈ id.
Proof. exact (Square_Thin x x p id). Qed.

(*
   * The seven hom-sets that carry no arrow.  [Square]'s hom types are
   the free ones, so these are the free emptiness results verbatim. 

   --------
   * 七个不包含箭头的同态集。[Square] 的同态类型是自由的，因此这些是自由空集的原文结果。
*)
Corollary square_no_hom_BA (p : Sq_B ~{Square}~> Sq_A) : False.
Proof. exact (free_square_no_path_BA p). Qed.

Corollary square_no_hom_CA (p : Sq_C ~{Square}~> Sq_A) : False.
Proof. exact (free_square_no_path_CA p). Qed.

Corollary square_no_hom_DA (p : Sq_D ~{Square}~> Sq_A) : False.
Proof. exact (free_square_no_path_DA p). Qed.

Corollary square_no_hom_BC (p : Sq_B ~{Square}~> Sq_C) : False.
Proof. exact (free_square_no_path_BC p). Qed.

Corollary square_no_hom_CB (p : Sq_C ~{Square}~> Sq_B) : False.
Proof. exact (free_square_no_path_CB p). Qed.

Corollary square_no_hom_DB (p : Sq_D ~{Square}~> Sq_B) : False.
Proof. exact (free_square_no_path_DB p). Qed.

Corollary square_no_hom_DC (p : Sq_D ~{Square}~> Sq_C) : False.
Proof. exact (free_square_no_path_DC p). Qed.

(*
   * ** The arrow count

   Mac Lane's exercise, answered.  [Square] is thin, so an arrow is
   determined by its endpoints, and counting arrows is counting the
   ordered pairs of nodes whose hom-set is inhabited.  The enumeration
   is a duplicate-free list, proved sound and complete. 

   --------
   * ** 箭头计数

   Mac Lane 的练习，已解答。[Square] 很稀薄，因此一个箭头由其端点决定，计数箭头就是计数那些同态集非空的节点有序对。枚举是一个无重复列表，并证明了其正确性和完整性。
*)

(*
   * Membership in a literal list, proved by walking it: try the head,
   otherwise step past it.  The walk terminates because [right] fails at
   the empty tail. 

   --------
   * 在字面列表中的成员，通过遍历它来证明：尝试获取头部，否则跳过它。遍历会终止，因为 [right] 在空尾部处失败。
*)
Local Ltac wsq_in := simpl; repeat (try (left; reflexivity); right).

Definition wsq_nodes : list SquareNode := Sq_A :: Sq_B :: Sq_C :: Sq_D :: nil.

Lemma wsq_nodes_complete (x : SquareNode) : In x wsq_nodes.
Proof. destruct x; wsq_in. Qed.

Lemma wsq_nodes_nodup : NoDup wsq_nodes.
Proof. repeat constructor; simpl; intuition congruence. Qed.

Definition wsq_all_pairs : list (SquareNode * SquareNode) :=
  list_prod wsq_nodes wsq_nodes.

Example wsq_all_pairs_16 : length wsq_all_pairs = 16%nat := eq_refl.

Lemma wsq_all_pairs_complete (x y : SquareNode) : In (x, y) wsq_all_pairs.
Proof.
  apply in_prod; apply wsq_nodes_complete.
Qed.

(*
   * The nine inhabited endpoint pairs: the four loops, the four sides,
   and the diagonal. 

   --------
   * 九个有人居住的端点对：四个环、四条边以及对角线。
*)
Definition wsq_pairs : list (SquareNode * SquareNode) :=
  (Sq_A, Sq_A) :: (Sq_B, Sq_B) :: (Sq_C, Sq_C) :: (Sq_D, Sq_D) ::
  (Sq_A, Sq_B) :: (Sq_A, Sq_C) :: (Sq_B, Sq_D) :: (Sq_C, Sq_D) ::
  (Sq_A, Sq_D) :: nil.

Lemma wsq_pairs_nodup : NoDup wsq_pairs.
Proof. repeat constructor; simpl; intuition congruence. Qed.

(** Soundness: each listed pair really does carry an arrow. / 稳健性：每个列出的配对确实存在箭头。 *)
Theorem wsq_pairs_sound (q : SquareNode * SquareNode) :
  In q wsq_pairs → fst q ~{Square}~> snd q.
Proof.
  destruct q as [x y]; intro H; destruct x, y; simpl in H;
    solve [ exact id
          | exact square_f | exact square_g
          | exact square_h | exact square_k
          | exact square_diagonal
          | exfalso; intuition congruence ].
Qed.

(** Completeness: no other pair does. / 完整性：没有其他组合能做到。 *)
Theorem wsq_pairs_complete (x y : SquareNode) :
  (x ~{Square}~> y) → In (x, y) wsq_pairs.
Proof.
  intro p; destruct x, y;
    solve [ wsq_in | exfalso; exact (wsq_classify _ _ p) ].
Qed.

(*
   * The count, as a number.  [wsq_homcount] gives the number of
   [≈]-classes of arrows between each pair of nodes; it is 1 exactly on
   the listed pairs and 0 elsewhere ([wsq_homcount_pairs]), and the
   per-pair statements above say what those numbers mean. 

   --------
   * 计数，以数字表示。[wsq_homcount] 给出了每对节点之间箭头的 [≈] 类的数量；在列出的节点对上恰好为 1，其余为 0（[wsq_homcount_pairs]），上述每对节点的说明则说明了这些数字的含义。
*)
Definition wsq_homcount (x y : SquareNode) : nat :=
  match x, y with
  | Sq_A, Sq_A => 1 | Sq_A, Sq_B => 1 | Sq_A, Sq_C => 1 | Sq_A, Sq_D => 1
  | Sq_B, Sq_B => 1 | Sq_B, Sq_D => 1
  | Sq_C, Sq_C => 1 | Sq_C, Sq_D => 1
  | Sq_D, Sq_D => 1
  | _, _ => 0
  end.

Lemma wsq_homcount_pairs (x y : SquareNode) :
  (wsq_homcount x y = 1%nat) ↔ In (x, y) wsq_pairs.
Proof.
  destruct x, y; split; intro H;
    solve [ reflexivity | wsq_in | discriminate
          | exfalso; simpl in H; intuition congruence ].
Qed.

Definition square_arrow_total : nat :=
  fold_right (fun q n => wsq_homcount (fst q) (snd q) + n)%nat 0%nat
    wsq_all_pairs.

(** Mac Lane §II.8 Exercise 1: nine arrows. / 麦克雷恩 §II.8 练习 1：九支箭。 *)
Theorem square_arrow_total_9 : square_arrow_total = 9%nat.
Proof. reflexivity. Qed.

Definition square_identity_total : nat :=
  fold_right (fun x n => wsq_homcount x x + n)%nat 0%nat wsq_nodes.

(** ...four of them identities. / ……其中四个身份。 *)
Theorem square_identity_total_4 : square_identity_total = 4%nat.
Proof. reflexivity. Qed.

Definition square_nonidentity_total : nat :=
  (square_arrow_total - square_identity_total)%nat.

(** ...and five of them not. / ...而其中五个不是。 *)
Theorem square_nonidentity_total_5 : square_nonidentity_total = 5%nat.
Proof. reflexivity. Qed.

(*
   * The five non-identity arrows, named, with their endpoint pairs
   pairwise distinct — so they are five arrows and not fewer.  (In a
   category the total arrow collection is the disjoint union of the
   hom-sets, so distinct endpoint pairs already give distinct arrows;
   the content is that no two of the five share a hom-set, which the
   [NoDup] records, together with the fact that none of them is an
   endomorphism, hence none is an identity.) 

   --------
   * 这五个非恒等箭头已经被命名，它们的端点对两两不同——所以它们是五个箭头，而不是更少。（在一个范畴中，总箭头集合是同态集的离散并，因此不同的端点对已经意味着箭头不同；内容在于这五个箭头中没有两个共享同态集，[NoDup] 记录了这一点，同时也记录了它们都不是自同构，因此没有一个是恒等箭头。）
*)
Definition wsq_nonidentity_pairs : list (SquareNode * SquareNode) :=
  (Sq_A, Sq_B) :: (Sq_A, Sq_C) :: (Sq_B, Sq_D) :: (Sq_C, Sq_D) ::
  (Sq_A, Sq_D) :: nil.

Example wsq_nonidentity_pairs_5 : length wsq_nonidentity_pairs = 5%nat := eq_refl.

Lemma wsq_nonidentity_pairs_nodup : NoDup wsq_nonidentity_pairs.
Proof. repeat constructor; simpl; intuition congruence. Qed.

Lemma wsq_nonidentity_not_endo (q : SquareNode * SquareNode) :
  In q wsq_nonidentity_pairs → fst q = snd q → False.
Proof.
  destruct q as [x y]; destruct x, y; simpl;
    solve [ intros _ H; discriminate H
          | intro H; exfalso; intuition congruence ].
Qed.

(*
   * ** The free square has ten arrows

   The same count run before the quotient.  The A → D hom-set has TWO
   elements there, and they are provably distinct
   ([free_square_diagonals_distinct], [Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v]),
   so [Square] merges exactly one pair of arrows and nothing else. 

   --------
   * ** 自由方形有十个箭头

   在商之前运行相同的计数。A → D 的同态集有两个元素，并且它们是可证明不同的
   （[free_square_diagonals_distinct]，[Construction/Free/Quiver/Presented.v]），
   因此 [Square] 精确地合并了一对箭头，而其他的没有。
*)

Definition wsq_free_homcount (x y : SquareNode) : nat :=
  match x, y with
  | Sq_A, Sq_A => 1 | Sq_A, Sq_B => 1 | Sq_A, Sq_C => 1 | Sq_A, Sq_D => 2
  | Sq_B, Sq_B => 1 | Sq_B, Sq_D => 1
  | Sq_C, Sq_C => 1 | Sq_C, Sq_D => 1
  | Sq_D, Sq_D => 1
  | _, _ => 0
  end.

Definition free_square_arrow_total : nat :=
  fold_right (fun q n => wsq_free_homcount (fst q) (snd q) + n)%nat 0%nat
    wsq_all_pairs.

Theorem free_square_arrow_total_10 : free_square_arrow_total = 10%nat.
Proof. reflexivity. Qed.

(*
   * The single merge, stated on both sides: distinct upstairs, equal
   downstairs.  [free_square_diagonals_distinct] is stated for [≈] in
   the free category; the Leibniz form follows, since equal paths are
   equivalent. 

   --------
   * 双方都说明了单次合并：楼上不同，楼下相同。在自由范畴中，[free_square_diagonals_distinct] 被说明为 [≈]；Leibniz 形式随之而来，因为相等的路径是等价的。
*)
Theorem free_square_diagonals_neq : square_diag_fh = square_diag_gk → False.
Proof.
  intro H; apply free_square_diagonals_distinct; rewrite H; reflexivity.
Qed.

Theorem square_quotient_merges_one :
  ((square_diag_fh = square_diag_gk → False) *
   @equiv _ (@homset Square Sq_A Sq_D) square_diag_fh square_diag_gk)%type.
Proof. exact (free_square_diagonals_neq, square_relation_holds). Qed.

(** The arithmetic of the merge, as a computation. / 合并的算术，作为一种计算。 *)
Example square_merge_arithmetic :
  (free_square_arrow_total - square_arrow_total)%nat = 1%nat := eq_refl.

(*
   * ** Two invariants, independent of the classification

   Everything above rests on [wsq_classify].  A count that rests on a
   single lemma is a count that says nothing if that lemma is silently
   weakened, so this section adds two invariants that are proved from
   the path structure alone and never mention it.  They are the shape
   of [Construction/Free/Quiver/Examples.v]'s [chain_e10_length]: a
   numerical quantity attached to each arrow, which a change to the
   PRESENTATION or to the closure machinery would have to violate
   loudly.  Not a collapse of this category — see the precision note
   below, which is deliberately stronger than this sentence.

   THEY ARE COMPLEMENTARY, and neither subsumes the other.  RANK rules
   out five of the seven empty hom-sets, by arithmetic on the endpoints
   alone; it cannot see the other two (B and C have the same rank —
   [wsq_rank_cannot_decide_BC] records exactly where the argument
   stops), and it cannot separate the two diagonals, both being
   two-step, which is why [free_square_diagonals_neq] discriminates on
   the INTERMEDIATE NODE instead.  LENGTH is invariant under the
   imposed congruence ([square_length_invariant]), so the quotient
   merged only equal-length paths.

   BE PRECISE ABOUT WHAT THE LENGTH INVARIANT BUYS HERE, because it is
   easy to overstate.  Its contrapositive [square_no_collapse] has NO
   instance in this category, and that is a fact about the square
   rather than a defect: by [square_hom_length] every arrow between a
   given pair of nodes already has the same length, namely the rank
   difference, so there is no parallel pair of differing lengths for it
   to separate.  What the invariant is for is that it is proved from
   the congruence closure ALONE — by induction on [CongClosure], using
   neither [wsq_classify] nor [Square_Thin] nor the count — so it fails
   loudly if the presentation is ever changed to relate paths of
   different lengths, or if the closure machinery stops being sound.
   That is the guard [Construction/Free/Quiver/Examples.v]'s
   [chain_e10_length] provides for the free case, carried across the
   quotient. 

   --------
   * ** 两个不依赖分类的不变量

   以上所有内容都依赖于 [wsq_classify]。一个仅依赖于单个引理的计数，如果该引理被默默削弱，那么这个计数就毫无意义，因此本节增加了两个仅从路径结构本身证明出来且从不提及它的不变量。它们是 [Construction/Free/Quiver/Examples.v] 的 [chain_e10_length] 的形状：
   一个附加到每个箭头的数值量，对 PRESENTATION 或闭包机制的更改都必须明显地违反它。这不是该范畴的塌缩——参见下面的精确性说明，它故意比这句话更强。它们是互补的，并且没有一个包含另一个。RANK 仅通过端点的算术排除了七个空同态集中的五个；它无法识别其他两个（B 和 C 的秩相同——[wsq_rank_cannot_decide_BC] 精确记录了论证停止的位置），并且无法区分两个对角线，因为它们都是两步的，这就是为什么 [free_square_diagonals_neq] 改为在中间节点上进行区分。LENGTH 在施加的合同下是不变的（[square_length_invariant]），因此商只合并长度相等的路径。要准确说明长度不变量在这里的作用，因为很容易夸大其作用。它的逆命题 [square_no_collapse] 在这个类别中没有实例，这是关于平方的一个事实，而不是缺陷：根据 [square_hom_length]，任意一对节点之间的每条箭头已经具有相同的长度，也就是秩差，因此不存在它需要区分的长度不同的平行箭头。这个不变量的作用在于，它是仅从全等闭包证明出来的——通过对 [CongClosure] 的归纳，既没有使用 [wsq_classify]，也没有使用 [Square_Thin]，也没有使用计数——因此，如果展示方式被更改为关联不同长度的路径，或者闭包机制不再可靠，它就会明显失败。这就是 [Construction/Free/Quiver/Examples.v] 的 [chain_e10_length] 为自由情况下提供的保障，并在商中传递。
*)

(* * *** Rank: every edge raises it by exactly one / * *** 等级：每条边都会将其提升一阶 *)

Definition wsq_rank (x : SquareNode) : nat :=
  match x with Sq_A => 0 | Sq_B => 1 | Sq_C => 1 | Sq_D => 2 end.

Lemma wsq_edge_rank {x y : SquareNode} (e : SquareEdge x y) :
  wsq_rank y = S (wsq_rank x).
Proof. destruct e; reflexivity. Qed.

(*
   * Hence a path's length is exactly the rank it climbs.  The rank is
   written FIRST in the sum on purpose: at concrete endpoints the sum
   then reduces to a numeral applied to [S], so each corollary below
   closes by [discriminate] with no arithmetic decision procedure. 

   --------
   * 因此，一条路径的长度正好等于它所攀升的等级。等级在求和中特意写在最前面：在具体的端点上，这个和然后简化为一个作用于 [S] 的数字，因此下面的每个推论都以 [discriminate] 结束，而无需算术判定过程。
*)
Lemma wsq_path_rank (x y : SquareNode) (p : x ~{FreeSquare}~> y) :
  wsq_rank y = (wsq_rank x + tlist_length p)%nat.
Proof.
  induction p as [ | i j e p IH ]; simpl.
  - now rewrite PeanoNat.Nat.add_0_r.
  - rewrite IH, (wsq_edge_rank e); simpl.
    now rewrite PeanoNat.Nat.add_succ_r.
Qed.

(** Five of the seven empty hom-sets, re-derived by arithmetic alone. / 七个空同态集中的五个，仅通过算术重新推导出来。 *)
Corollary wsq_rank_no_path_BA (p : Sq_B ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_A) : False.
Proof. pose proof (wsq_path_rank _ _ p) as H; discriminate H. Qed.

Corollary wsq_rank_no_path_CA (p : Sq_C ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_A) : False.
Proof. pose proof (wsq_path_rank _ _ p) as H; discriminate H. Qed.

Corollary wsq_rank_no_path_DA (p : Sq_D ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_A) : False.
Proof. pose proof (wsq_path_rank _ _ p) as H; discriminate H. Qed.

Corollary wsq_rank_no_path_DB (p : Sq_D ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_B) : False.
Proof. pose proof (wsq_path_rank _ _ p) as H; discriminate H. Qed.

Corollary wsq_rank_no_path_DC (p : Sq_D ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_C) : False.
Proof. pose proof (wsq_path_rank _ _ p) as H; discriminate H. Qed.

(*
   * The two rank cannot decide: [Sq_B] and [Sq_C] have the same rank, so
   the argument above degenerates to [tlist_length p = 0] and stops.
   They are supplied by the classification instead, and are stated here
   only to record that the rank route is INCOMPLETE — the two proofs
   below are [wsq_classify]'s, not rank's. 

   --------
   * 两个秩无法决定：[Sq_B] 和 [Sq_C] 的秩相同，因此上述论证退化为 [tlist_length p = 0] 并停止。它们改由分类提供，这里说明只是为了记录秩途径是不完整的——下面的两个证明属于 [wsq_classify]，而不是秩的。
*)
Corollary wsq_rank_cannot_decide_BC (p : Sq_B ~{FreeSquare}~> Sq_C) :
  tlist_length p = 0%nat.
Proof.
  pose proof (wsq_path_rank _ _ p) as H; simpl in H.
  now injection H.
Qed.

(*
   * Every arrow between a given pair of nodes climbs exactly the rank
   difference, so all of them have the SAME length.  Stated at
   [Square], where it holds because the quotient does not change the
   hom types. 

   --------
   * 给定一对节点之间的每个箭头恰好上升节点等级的差，因此它们的长度完全相同。在 [Square] 中说明了这一点，因为商不会改变 Hom 类型。
*)
Theorem square_hom_length (x y : SquareNode) (p : x ~{Square}~> y) :
  (wsq_rank x + tlist_length p)%nat = wsq_rank y.
Proof. symmetry; exact (wsq_path_rank x y p). Qed.

(* * *** Length: invariant under the imposed congruence / * *** 长度：在施加的同余下不变 *)

(*
   * Equivalent paths of the free category have equal length —
   [tlist'_equiv_lengths] ([Construction/Free/Quiver.v]) at this
   quiver. 

   --------
   * 自由范畴的等价路径具有相等的长度——
   在这个向矢图中，[tlist'_equiv_lengths]（[Construction/Free/Quiver.v]）。
*)
Lemma wsq_equiv_length {x y : SquareNode} (p q : x ~{FreeSquare}~> y) :
  p ≈ q → tlist_length p = tlist_length q.
Proof. intro H; exact (tlist'_equiv_lengths _ _ _ _ _ _ _ H). Qed.

(*
   * The single imposed equation relates two paths of the SAME length —
   both diagonals are two-step — which is what makes length survive the
   quotient. 

   --------
   * 单一施加的方程关联了两个长度相同的路径——两条对角线都是两步——这就是长度在除法中得以保留的原因。
*)
Lemma wsq_relation_length {x y : SquareNode}
  (p q : x ~{FreeSquare}~> y) (Hr : fe_rel SquareEqns x y p q) :
  tlist_length p = tlist_length q.
Proof.
  destruct Hr as [i [Hp Hq]].
  destruct x, y; simpl in i; try solve [ exact (Fin.case0 _ i) ].
  simpl in Hp, Hq.
  rewrite (wsq_equiv_length _ _ Hp), (wsq_equiv_length _ _ Hq).
  reflexivity.
Qed.

(*
   * Composition in a free category is path concatenation, so its length
   is the sum.  Stated over an arbitrary quiver, which is what makes it
   match the congruence closure's [cc_comp] goal — there the ambient
   category prints as [FreeOnQuiver (fp_quiver SquarePresentation)]
   rather than through this file's [FreeSquare] abbreviation. 

   --------
   * 在自由范畴中的复合是路径拼接，因此它的长度是总和。在任意箭图上陈述时，这正是使它与同余闭包的 [cc_comp] 目标匹配的原因——在那里，环境范畴显示为 [FreeOnQuiver (fp_quiver SquarePresentation)]，而不是通过此文件的 [FreeSquare] 缩写。
*)
Lemma wsq_comp_length {G : Quiver} {x y z : FreeOnQuiver G}
  (f : y ~> z) (g : x ~> y) :
  tlist_length (f ∘ g) = (tlist_length g + tlist_length f)%nat.
Proof. exact (tlist_app_length g f). Qed.

(*
   * So [Square] is GRADED by path length: equivalent arrows have equal
   length.  It is proved by induction on the congruence closure itself,
   using none of [wsq_classify], [Square_Thin] or the count — that
   independence is the point.  It is NOT a statement a collapse of this
   category would break: by [square_hom_length] every parallel pair
   already has equal length, so the conclusion holds unconditionally
   here and any identification of parallel arrows satisfies it.  What
   it guards is the PRESENTATION and the closure machinery; see the
   precision note in the section header. 

   --------
   * 所以 [Square] 是按路径长度分级的：等价箭头长度相等。通过对同余闭包本身的归纳证明这一点，过程中未使用 [wsq_classify]、[Square_Thin] 或计数——关键在于独立性。这并不是说，如果该范畴发生塌缩就会被破坏的陈述：根据 [square_hom_length]，每对平行箭头已经具有相等的长度，因此结论在此无条件成立，任何平行箭头的识别都满足这一点。它所保护的是表示法和闭包机制；参见章节标题中的精确性说明。
*)
Theorem square_length_invariant {x y : SquareNode} (p q : x ~{Square}~> y) :
  p ≈ q → tlist_length p = tlist_length q.
Proof.
  intro H.
  induction H as [ x y p q Hr | x y p q He | x y p q _ IH
                 | x y p q r _ IH1 _ IH2 | x y z f f' g g' _ IH1 _ IH2 ].
  - exact (wsq_relation_length p q Hr).
  - exact (wsq_equiv_length p q He).
  - now symmetry.
  - now transitivity (tlist_length q).
  - rewrite !wsq_comp_length.
    now rewrite IH1, IH2.
Qed.

(*
   * The contrapositive, which is the form a reader wants: arrows of
   different length are never identified. 

   --------
   * 逆命题，这是读者想要的形式：不同长度的箭头从不被认同。
*)
Corollary square_no_collapse {x y : SquareNode} (p q : x ~{Square}~> y) :
  (tlist_length p = tlist_length q → False) → p ≈ q → False.
Proof. intros Hne H; exact (Hne (square_length_invariant p q H)). Qed.

(*
   * *** The diagonal is a composite, measured

   Each generator is a one-step path and the diagonal a two-step one,
   by computation. 

   --------
   * *** 对角线是一个复合，经过测量

   每个生成元都是一步路径，对角线是两步路径，
   通过计算得出。
*)
Example square_f_length : tlist_length square_f = 1%nat := eq_refl.
Example square_g_length : tlist_length square_g = 1%nat := eq_refl.
Example square_h_length : tlist_length square_h = 1%nat := eq_refl.
Example square_k_length : tlist_length square_k = 1%nat := eq_refl.

Example square_diagonal_length : tlist_length square_diagonal = 2%nat := eq_refl.

(** Every generator's image is one step, uniformly. / 每个生成器的图像都是一步，均匀地。 *)
Lemma square_gen_length {x y : SquareNode} (e : SquareEdge x y) :
  tlist_length (@pgen SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) x y e) = 1%nat.
Proof. reflexivity. Qed.

(*
   * ...and length being an invariant, that survives the quotient: ANY
   arrow of [Square] equivalent to the diagonal is a two-step path, so
   the diagonal is a composite at every representative and not a
   generator in disguise. 

   --------
   * …并且长度作为不变量，在商结构中保持不变：[Square] 中任何与对角线等价的箭头都是一个两步路径，因此对角线在每个代表中都是一个复合，而不是伪装的生成元。
*)
Theorem square_diagonal_is_two_steps (p : Sq_A ~{Square}~> Sq_D) :
  p ≈ square_diagonal → tlist_length p = 2%nat.
Proof.
  intro H.
  now rewrite (square_length_invariant p square_diagonal H).
Qed.

(*
   * The other half of "not a generator", from the presentation rather
   than from the grading: the quiver has no edge A → D at all. 

   --------
   * “不是生成器”的另一半，不是来自评分而是来自演示：这个箭袋根本没有边 A → D。
*)
Lemma square_no_diagonal_edge (e : SquareEdge Sq_A Sq_D) : False.
Proof. inversion e. Qed.

(*
   * ** The index shape: functors out of [Square] are commutative squares

   Mac Lane's third clause, and Riehl's Example 1.6.6.  A commutative
   square in [C] is four objects, four morphisms and one equation. 

   --------
   * ** 指数形状：从  [Square]  出发的函子是交换平方

   Mac Lane 的第三条款，以及 Riehl 的例子 1.6.6。在  [C]  中的一个交换平方是四个对象、四个态射和一个方程。
*)

Record CommutingSquare (C : Category) : Type := {
  csq_a : C;
  csq_b : C;
  csq_c : C;
  csq_d : C;
  csq_f : csq_a ~> csq_b;
  csq_g : csq_a ~> csq_c;
  csq_h : csq_b ~> csq_d;
  csq_k : csq_c ~> csq_d;
  csq_commutes : csq_h ∘ csq_f ≈ csq_k ∘ csq_g
}.

Arguments csq_a {C} _.
Arguments csq_b {C} _.
Arguments csq_c {C} _.
Arguments csq_d {C} _.
Arguments csq_f {C} _.
Arguments csq_g {C} _.
Arguments csq_h {C} _.
Arguments csq_k {C} _.
Arguments csq_commutes {C} _.

Section IndexShape.

Context {C : Category}.

Definition csq_node (S : CommutingSquare C) (n : SquareNode) : C :=
  match n with
  | Sq_A => csq_a S
  | Sq_B => csq_b S
  | Sq_C => csq_c S
  | Sq_D => csq_d S
  end.

Definition csq_edgemap (S : CommutingSquare C) (x y : SquareNode)
  (e : SquareEdge x y) : csq_node S x ~> csq_node S y :=
  match e in SquareEdge a b return csq_node S a ~> csq_node S b with
  | Sq_f => csq_f S
  | Sq_g => csq_g S
  | Sq_h => csq_h S
  | Sq_k => csq_k S
  end.

Definition square_quiver_hom (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  QuiverHomomorphism SquareQuiver (QuiverOfCat C).
Proof.
  unshelve eapply Build_QuiverHomomorphism.
  - exact (csq_node S).
  - exact (csq_edgemap S).
  - intros x y u v Huv; simpl in Huv; subst; reflexivity.
Defined.

(*
   * The one imposed relation is merged: that is exactly the square's
   commuting equation, modulo the trailing identity a [tlist] fold
   leaves behind. 

   --------
   * 所施加的关系已合并：那正是方形的交换方程，模掉尾随的恒等式 a  [tlist] 折叠留下的部分。
*)
Lemma square_quiver_hom_merges (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  ∀ x y (p q : x ~{FreeSquare}~> y), fe_rel SquareEqns x y p q →
    fmap[@InducedFunctor SquareQuiver C (square_quiver_hom S)] p
      ≈ fmap[@InducedFunctor SquareQuiver C (square_quiver_hom S)] q.
Proof.
  intros x y p q [i [Hp Hq]].
  destruct x, y; simpl in i; try solve [ exact (Fin.case0 _ i) ].
  simpl in Hp, Hq; rewrite Hp, Hq; simpl.
  rewrite !id_left.
  exact (csq_commutes S).
Qed.

(** The functor a commutative square names. / 函子命名一个交换方格。 *)
Definition SquareFunctor (S : CommutingSquare C) : Square ⟶ C :=
  @PresentedFunctor SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) C
    (square_quiver_hom S) (square_quiver_hom_merges S).

(** It has the given objects, on the nose. / 它正好有给定的物体。 *)
Example SquareFunctor_A (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  fobj[SquareFunctor S] Sq_A = csq_a S := eq_refl.
Example SquareFunctor_B (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  fobj[SquareFunctor S] Sq_B = csq_b S := eq_refl.
Example SquareFunctor_C (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  fobj[SquareFunctor S] Sq_C = csq_c S := eq_refl.
Example SquareFunctor_D (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  fobj[SquareFunctor S] Sq_D = csq_d S := eq_refl.

(** ...and the given morphisms, up to the fold's trailing identity. / ……以及给定的态射，直到 fold 的尾随恒等。 *)
Lemma SquareFunctor_f (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  fmap[SquareFunctor S] square_f ≈ csq_f S.
Proof.
  exact (@PresentedFunctor_gen SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) C
           (square_quiver_hom S) (square_quiver_hom_merges S) _ _ Sq_f).
Qed.

Lemma SquareFunctor_g (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  fmap[SquareFunctor S] square_g ≈ csq_g S.
Proof.
  exact (@PresentedFunctor_gen SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) C
           (square_quiver_hom S) (square_quiver_hom_merges S) _ _ Sq_g).
Qed.

Lemma SquareFunctor_h (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  fmap[SquareFunctor S] square_h ≈ csq_h S.
Proof.
  exact (@PresentedFunctor_gen SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) C
           (square_quiver_hom S) (square_quiver_hom_merges S) _ _ Sq_h).
Qed.

Lemma SquareFunctor_k (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  fmap[SquareFunctor S] square_k ≈ csq_k S.
Proof.
  exact (@PresentedFunctor_gen SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) C
           (square_quiver_hom S) (square_quiver_hom_merges S) _ _ Sq_k).
Qed.

(*
   * The converse: a functor out of [Square] IS a commutative square, the
   equation coming from [square_commutes] under [fmap_respects]. 

   --------
   * 反过来：一个来自 [Square] 的函子是一个交换方，方程来自 [square_commutes] 在 [fmap_respects] 下。
*)
Lemma functor_square_commutes (F : Square ⟶ C) :
  fmap[F] square_h ∘ fmap[F] square_f ≈ fmap[F] square_k ∘ fmap[F] square_g.
Proof.
  rewrite <- !fmap_comp.
  apply fmap_respects.
  exact square_commutes.
Qed.

Definition CommutingSquareOfFunctor (F : Square ⟶ C) : CommutingSquare C := {|
  csq_a := fobj[F] Sq_A;
  csq_b := fobj[F] Sq_B;
  csq_c := fobj[F] Sq_C;
  csq_d := fobj[F] Sq_D;
  csq_f := fmap[F] square_f;
  csq_g := fmap[F] square_g;
  csq_h := fmap[F] square_h;
  csq_k := fmap[F] square_k;
  csq_commutes := functor_square_commutes F
|}.

(*
   * Round trip one, on the square side: the objects come back on the
   nose and the morphisms up to [≈]. 

   --------
   * 往返一次，在平方面上：物体沿着鼻子返回，而态射到 [≈]。
*)
Example square_round_obj_a (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  csq_a (CommutingSquareOfFunctor (SquareFunctor S)) = csq_a S := eq_refl.
Example square_round_obj_b (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  csq_b (CommutingSquareOfFunctor (SquareFunctor S)) = csq_b S := eq_refl.
Example square_round_obj_c (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  csq_c (CommutingSquareOfFunctor (SquareFunctor S)) = csq_c S := eq_refl.
Example square_round_obj_d (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  csq_d (CommutingSquareOfFunctor (SquareFunctor S)) = csq_d S := eq_refl.

Theorem square_round_morphisms (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  ((csq_f (CommutingSquareOfFunctor (SquareFunctor S)) ≈ csq_f S) *
   (csq_g (CommutingSquareOfFunctor (SquareFunctor S)) ≈ csq_g S) *
   (csq_h (CommutingSquareOfFunctor (SquareFunctor S)) ≈ csq_h S) *
   (csq_k (CommutingSquareOfFunctor (SquareFunctor S)) ≈ csq_k S))%type.
Proof.
  repeat split;
    [ exact (SquareFunctor_f S) | exact (SquareFunctor_g S)
    | exact (SquareFunctor_h S) | exact (SquareFunctor_k S) ].
Qed.

(*
   * Round trip two, on the functor side: the functor rebuilt from a
   functor's own square agrees with it on objects and on every
   morphism.  Stated at STRICT strength — Leibniz on objects, a
   [hom_cast] conjugation on morphisms, which is [StrictCat]'s functor
   equality ([Functor_StrictEq_Setoid], via [strict_of_hom_cast]) —
   because that is the strength [PresentedFunctor_unique] supplies and
   it is stronger than a [Cat]-level reading, not weaker.

   The object agreement is [eq_refl] AT EACH OF THE FOUR NODES but not
   uniformly in a variable node: [csq_node] is a match, so
   [csq_node (CommutingSquareOfFunctor F) x] reduces to [fobj[F] x]
   only once [x] is a constructor.  Hence the family below is a
   four-branch match rather than [fun _ => eq_refl]; that is a
   statement about reduction, not a weakening. 

   --------
   * 往返两次，在函子方面：从一个函子的自身平方重建的函子，在对象和每一个态射上都与它一致。以严格强度表述——对象上的莱布尼茨，态射上的 [hom_cast] 共轭，这是 [StrictCat] 的函子等式（[Functor_StrictEq_Setoid]，通过 [strict_of_hom_cast]）——因为这是 [PresentedFunctor_unique] 提供的强度，并且它比 [Cat] 级别的解释更强，而不是更弱。

   对象的一致性在四个节点的每一个都是 [eq_refl]，但在变量节点上不统一：[csq_node] 是匹配，因此 [csq_node (CommutingSquareOfFunctor F) x] 简化为 [fobj[F] x] 仅当 [x] 是构造函数时。因此，下面的族是一个四分支匹配，而不是 [fun _ => eq_refl]；这是一个关于归约的陈述，而不是关于弱化的。
*)
Definition square_round_obj (F : Square ⟶ C) (x : SquareNode) :
  fobj[F] x = csq_node (CommutingSquareOfFunctor F) x :=
  match x with
  | Sq_A => eq_refl
  | Sq_B => eq_refl
  | Sq_C => eq_refl
  | Sq_D => eq_refl
  end.

Theorem square_functor_round (F : Square ⟶ C) :
  ∀ (x y : SquareNode) (p : x ~{Square}~> y),
    hom_cast (square_round_obj F x) (square_round_obj F y) (fmap[F] p)
      ≈ fmap[SquareFunctor (CommutingSquareOfFunctor F)] p.
Proof.
  apply (@PresentedFunctor_unique SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) C
           (square_quiver_hom (CommutingSquareOfFunctor F))
           (square_quiver_hom_merges (CommutingSquareOfFunctor F))
           F (square_round_obj F)).
  intros x y e; destruct e; reflexivity.
Qed.

(*
   * ...and the same, packaged as an equality of functors in
   [StrictCat]. 

   --------
   * ...并且相同，作为 [StrictCat] 中函子的一致性来打包。
*)
Theorem square_functor_round_strict (F : Square ⟶ C) :
  @equiv _ (@Functor_StrictEq_Setoid Square C)
    F (SquareFunctor (CommutingSquareOfFunctor F)).
Proof.
  apply (strict_of_hom_cast F (SquareFunctor (CommutingSquareOfFunctor F))
           (square_round_obj F)).
  exact (square_functor_round F).
Qed.

(*
   * The universal property, bundled: to give a functor out of [Square]
   is exactly to give a commutative square, and the functor is unique
   at strict strength. 

   --------
   * 通用性质，捆绑：给出一个从 [Square] 出发的函子，正是给出了一个交换方格，并且在严格强度下该函子是唯一的。
*)
Theorem square_universal (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  { F : Square ⟶ C &
  { Hobj : ∀ x : SquareNode, fobj[F] x = csq_node S x &
    (((hom_cast (Hobj Sq_A) (Hobj Sq_B) (fmap[F] square_f) ≈ csq_f S) *
      (hom_cast (Hobj Sq_A) (Hobj Sq_C) (fmap[F] square_g) ≈ csq_g S) *
      (hom_cast (Hobj Sq_B) (Hobj Sq_D) (fmap[F] square_h) ≈ csq_h S) *
      (hom_cast (Hobj Sq_C) (Hobj Sq_D) (fmap[F] square_k) ≈ csq_k S)) *
     (∀ (K : Square ⟶ C) (Hobj' : ∀ x : SquareNode, fobj[K] x = csq_node S x),
        (∀ (x y : SquareNode) (e : SquareEdge x y),
           hom_cast (Hobj' x) (Hobj' y)
             (fmap[K] (@pgen SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) x y e))
             ≈ csq_edgemap S x y e) →
        ∀ (x y : SquareNode) (p : x ~{Square}~> y),
          hom_cast (Hobj' x) (Hobj' y) (fmap[K] p)
            ≈ hom_cast (Hobj x) (Hobj y) (fmap[F] p)))%type } }.
Proof.
  exists (SquareFunctor S), (fun _ => eq_refl).
  split; [ repeat split | ].
  - exact (SquareFunctor_f S).
  - exact (SquareFunctor_g S).
  - exact (SquareFunctor_h S).
  - exact (SquareFunctor_k S).
  - intros K Hobj' Hgen x y p.
    exact (@PresentedFunctor_unique SquareQuiver (fe_rel SquareEqns) C
             (square_quiver_hom S) (square_quiver_hom_merges S)
             K Hobj' Hgen x y p).
Qed.

(*
   * ** A commutative square is a morphism of the arrow category

   [Construction/Arrow.v] defines [Arrow C] as the comma category
   [Id[C] ↓ Id[C]]: its objects are the morphisms of [C] and its
   morphisms are exactly commuting squares.  So a functor out of
   [Square] and a morphism of [Arrow C] carry the same data, and the
   passage is a repackaging with no proof content beyond reassociating
   the commuting equation.  The square is read with its two VERTICAL
   sides as the arrow-category objects: [csq_g] : a → c and
   [csq_h] : b → d, connected by ([csq_f], [csq_k]). 

   --------
   * ** 交换方形是箭头范畴的一个态射

   [Construction/Arrow.v] 定义了 [Arrow C] 作为逗号范畴
   [Id[C]  ↓ Id [C] ]：它的对象是 [C] 的态射，其态射恰好是交换方形。因此，从
   [Square] 出发的函子和 [Arrow C] 的一个态射包含相同的数据，这个过程只是重新打包，并没有超出重新关联交换方程之外的证明内容。方形的阅读方式是将其两个垂直边作为箭头范畴的对象：[csq_g] ：a → c 和
   [csq_h] ：b → d，由 ([csq_f] , [csq_k]) 连接。
*)

Definition arrow_dom (S : CommutingSquare C) : @Arrow C :=
  ((csq_a S, csq_c S); csq_g S).

Definition arrow_cod (S : CommutingSquare C) : @Arrow C :=
  ((csq_b S, csq_d S); csq_h S).

Definition arrow_of_square (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  arrow_dom S ~{@Arrow C}~> arrow_cod S :=
  ((csq_f S, csq_k S); csq_commutes S).

Definition square_of_arrow {x y : @Arrow C} (u : x ~> y) : CommutingSquare C := {|
  csq_a := fst (``x);
  csq_b := fst (``y);
  csq_c := snd (``x);
  csq_d := snd (``y);
  csq_f := fst (``u);
  csq_g := `2 x;
  csq_h := `2 y;
  csq_k := snd (``u);
  csq_commutes := `2 u
|}.

(*
   * Round trip one, from the square side: a Leibniz equality of the
   whole record, the strongest form available.  It holds by [eq_refl]
   because [CommutingSquare] has primitive projections (hence record
   eta) and every component is a projection of an explicitly built
   pair. 

   --------
   * 往返一次，从平方边开始：整个记录的莱布尼茨等式，这是可用的最强形式。它通过 [eq_refl] 成立，因为 [CommutingSquare] 有原始投影（因此有记录 eta），并且每个组件都是明确定义的对的投影。
*)
Example square_arrow_round (S : CommutingSquare C) :
  square_of_arrow (arrow_of_square S) = S := eq_refl.

(*
   * Round trip two, from the arrow side.  The two endpoint objects come
   back on the nose — but only after the underlying PAIR is exposed:
   Coq's [prod] carries no eta, so [(fst ``x, snd ``x)] is not
   convertible to [``x] for a variable [x].  That is a statement about
   [prod], not a weakening; the equalities below are Leibniz. 

   --------
   * 往返两次，从箭头侧。两个端点对象正好返回——但只有在底层 PAIR 被暴露之后：Coq 的 [prod] 没有 eta，因此 [(fst ``x, snd ``x)] 对于变量 [x] 不能转换为 [``x]。这是关于 [prod] 的陈述，而不是弱化；下面的等式是 Leibniz 的。
*)
Lemma arrow_square_round_dom (x y : @Arrow C) (u : x ~> y) :
  arrow_dom (square_of_arrow u) = x.
Proof. destruct x as [[a c] v]; reflexivity. Qed.

Lemma arrow_square_round_cod (x y : @Arrow C) (u : x ~> y) :
  arrow_cod (square_of_arrow u) = y.
Proof. destruct y as [[b d] w]; reflexivity. Qed.

(*
   * ...and so does the morphism.  Stated with the endpoints already in
   pair form, since otherwise the two sides do not even have the same
   type. 

   --------
   * ……同样地，态射也是如此。已将端点用配对形式表示，否则两边的类型甚至都不相同。
*)
Lemma arrow_square_round_mor (a b c d : C) (v : a ~> c) (w : b ~> d)
  (u : ((a, c); v) ~{@Arrow C}~> ((b, d); w)) :
  arrow_of_square (square_of_arrow u) = u.
Proof. destruct u as [[p q] Hu]; reflexivity. Qed.

End IndexShape.

Arguments SquareFunctor {C} _.
Arguments CommutingSquareOfFunctor {C} _.
Arguments arrow_dom {C} _.
Arguments arrow_cod {C} _.
Arguments arrow_of_square {C} _.
Arguments square_of_arrow {C x y} _.
